# What never enters the build context (task T-602).
#
# Without this file the context is the entire working tree: the dataset, the virtualenv, the
# git history, every MLflow run. That is slow to upload on every build, and it puts
# third-party data and local secrets one careless COPY away from a published image (docs/09).
#
# NOTHING COPIED BY THE DOCKERFILE MAY BE LISTED HERE. `models/` and `reports/figures/` are
# both copied, so neither appears below. This is the same trap `.gcloudignore` sets by
# falling back to `.gitignore` (docs/12): an ignore file that hides the model gives you a
# green build and a container that cannot start, with no error until it is running.

# --- version control and CI ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# --- local environments and caches ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- secrets and local config: never in an image ---
.env
.env.local
kaggle.json
access_token
.kaggle/

# --- third-party data, logs, experiment tracking ---
data/
mlruns/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.log

# --- documentation and tooling: not runtime ---
docs/
notebooks/
design-system/
deploy/
tests/
scripts/
Makefile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
